# bandwidth-probe fixture — BASE IMAGES class (fedora-dev#322 / objective #311).
#
# Measures whether a second consecutive build re-pulls its base image. The cache under test is the
# local podman layer/blob store, which #311 records as covering this class incidentally ("the podman
# layer cache surviving the candidate `rmi`") — incidentally, and so with nothing protecting it. This
# arm is what would notice if that ever stopped being true.
#
# NO CACHEBUST HERE, deliberately — unlike the ospkg fixture. `FROM` resolves against the local store
# directly, so there is no layer-cache confound to defeat: build 2 costing zero bytes IS the property
# being measured, not an artifact of a step being skipped. Forcing a re-pull (`--pull=always`) would
# measure podman's manifest-check behaviour instead, which is not the objective's question.
#
# The COPY keeps the fixture's only network-touching step the base-image resolution, so the bytes this
# arm reports are attributable to this class and no other.
ARG FEDORA_VERSION=44
FROM registry.fedoraproject.org/fedora-minimal:${FEDORA_VERSION}

COPY marker /bandwidth-probe-baseimg
